From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] venus: Vulkan Video (decode and encode)

Venus had no Vulkan Video. With virglrenderer's patch 0008 the host's video
queues reach the guest: on NVIDIA that's NVDEC and NVENC (ffmpeg's h264_vulkan
and hevc_vulkan encode; checked against the source at 54-68 dB PSNR). Decoding (-hwaccel vulkan) of H.264, HEVC Main/Main 10, VP9
profiles 0/2 and AV1 Main 8/10-bit matches libavcodec bit for bit.

- venus-protocol regenerated with WinBoat's generator changes (the codec types
  of video.xml, VK_KHR_video_queue, video_decode/encode_queue, _h264, _h265, decode_av1 and
  decode_vp9,
  video_maintenance1/2, int8_t/int16_t, commands 1000-1015; the same as the
  host's).
- vn_video.c: physical-device video queries, sessions and session parameters
  (created synchronously), memory requirements and binding, encoded session
  parameters.
- vn_command_buffer.c: the five video coding commands.
- vn_physical_device.c: the extensions passed through as far as the host has
  them, the queue families' video properties, the maintenance1/2 and VP9
  decode features,
  and the video format features of NV12/P010 (the YCbCr feature mask dropped
  them, so no image could be a video picture).
- vn_query_pool.c: result-status-only and encode-feedback query pools without
  query feedback; results with VK_QUERY_RESULT_WITH_STATUS_BIT_KHR pass
  through as they are (adding the availability bit to them is invalid).
- vn_image.c: VkVideoProfileListInfoKHR survives the rewritten chain of an
  image with external memory.
